# Problematic E2E assertions

These four checks fail for a harness or platform reason. The product behavior around them can
stay. Do not add the assertion back, do not defer it, and do not spend another run trying to make
it pass.

## Web notification stream replay header

Do not assert `Last-Event-ID` / `last-event-id` on a Playwright-routed `EventSource` reconnect in
`apps/web/e2e/notifications-inbox.spec.ts`. The route runs before Chromium attaches that header, so
`request.headers()` is `undefined` even when the browser sent it. Do not restore the test titled
"When the stream reconnects after a new notification, it asks the server to replay from that
notification."

The rest of that spec still covers the inbox and the bell.

## iOS livestream rewind scrubber

Do not assert that `full-player-scrubber` becomes visible for `e2eLiveHlsRw01` in
`apps/mobile/e2e/livestream-player-controls.yaml`. AVPlayer reports that static EVENT playlist as a
file, so the rewind window stays empty for the whole wait. Do not add the skip-back, behind-live,
or resume-in-place steps that depend on that scrubber.

The flow still checks that an episode shows its duration and that a window too short to rewind
hides the scrubber.

## iOS landscape fullscreen Exit

Do not assert `video-fullscreen-exit` in `apps/mobile/e2e/video-transition.yaml`. The landscape
control stays at opacity 0, and iOS omits it from the accessibility tree. Do not tap
`video-fullscreen-tap` or `video-fullscreen` to reveal it.

The flow still checks the mini-player and full-player video surfaces and the collapse back to the
mini player.

## iOS cross-device "Sending to…" status

Do not assert `mini-player-remote-status` text `Sending to…` in
`apps/mobile/e2e/playback-cross-device.yaml`. That status is gone before Maestro samples the
screen. Assert `playback-transfer-failed-dialog` ("didn't respond"), which is the result that
stays on screen.

## What a later run does instead

When one of these fails, or when a plan asks for the same check: leave the assertion out. Say that
this rule retired it. Do not weaken it with a longer timeout, a retry, or a looser matcher.
